We establish the inequlities \begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
\prod_{i=1}^{n-1} \lambda_i^{f_i} \ll_{s, \epsilon, n} \begin{cases}
\left( \frac{S}{q_0} \frac{1}{D^{1-\epsilon}} \right)^{2s-1} & 0 < s \leq \frac{1}{2}, \\
\left( \frac{S}{q_0} \frac{1}{D^{1-\epsilon}} \right)^{2s-2} D^{\epsilon} & \frac{1}{2} < s \leq 1,
\end{cases}
\end{split}
\end{equation*}where the lower case lambda represents the number of isomorphism classes of orders in a number field with a specified Galois action, up to $q_0$ and with degree bounded below by $D$, given certain arithmetic conditions are met.

Given a differential module ${\mathcal M}$ defined by the operator $D$ and the action on ${\mathcal C}$, we say that $D$ is parametrized by another differential module $R$ if there exists a differential module ${\mathcal N}$ such that ${\mathcal M}$ is isomorphic to the tensor product of ${\mathcal N}$ and the module associated with $R$. In this case, we denote the relation as $D \sim_{{\mathcal C}} 
abla_{{\mathcal C}}$, where $
abla_{{\mathcal C}}$ is the standard operator associated with the differential module $R$. Our main result establishes that if $D \sim_{{\mathcal C}} 
abla_{{\mathcal C}}$ and the associated differential modules are smooth over a suitable open set, then the operators $D$ and $
abla_{{\mathcal C}}$ are analytically related within that open set.
